5,1,1,talk,Mizuki,,"To make a logical choice, we need to understand how previous projects actually performed. I suggest we prioritize user satisfaction and actual utility over mere budget figures. What do you all think?","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Victoria,,I agree with Mizuki. We should examine how these spaces are actually utilized and the impact of construction on daily operations. I'm particularly interested in the post-occupancy reviews and the timetable records for rooms out of service.,"{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,"While user satisfaction is a charming metric, I am more concerned with the ghosts of projects past—specifically, why they always seem to finish late. I'll look into the weather days in the site diaries and the delivery schedules.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Kenji,,I think we need to be honest about the money! Paper budgets often lie. I want to see the tender records over three budget cycles and the renewal reserve for equipment bought earlier.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Shunichi,,You're all focusing on the surface. What about the people actually keeping this place running? I'll look into the staffing posts since the hiring freeze and the bench technicians' weekly manual routines. Let's see who's actually doing the work.,"{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Victoria, I appreciate your support. Since we are all looking at different angles, I will focus on the Post-occupancy review ratings and the Booking data for specialist and general rooms to gauge actual demand.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, that sounds like a comprehensive approach. I will stick with my plan to examine the Timetable records on rooms out of service and the Post-occupancy review ratings to see how disruptions affect us.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we have a delightful division of labor. To ensure our chosen project doesn't become a permanent fixture of the landscape, I shall proceed with the weather days in the site diaries and the delivery schedules.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, you're right about the delays, but the costs usually jump too! I'm sticking with the tender records and the renewal reserve. I want to know if the prices we're seeing are actually realistic.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Shunichi,,It's almost touching how you all assume the buildings maintain themselves. I'll stick to my choices. Let's hope the data reveals the exhaustion that your spreadsheets conveniently ignore.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Mizuki,,"It seems we have a balanced set of priorities. By combining user feedback, operational costs, scheduling risks, and staffing constraints, we can avoid the mistakes of the past. Does anyone feel we've missed a critical data source?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Victoria,,"I believe we have covered the primary bases. However, I hope we remain mindful of how the physical changes we decide upon will integrate with the actual academic schedule once the work begins.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed, @Victoria. The gap between a theoretical timeline and the reality of a construction site is often where the real tragedy occurs. I suspect our findings will reveal some rather illuminating discrepancies.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Kenji,,"I'm just excited to see what we find! If the tender records show a big gap from the budgets, we'll have to be really careful. Let's make sure we don't ignore the hidden costs!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Shunichi,,"Hidden costs are one thing, Kenji, but the human cost is what usually breaks the system. I'm sure the data will be quite illuminating for all of us. I'm satisfied with my selections.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Mizuki,,"Then it is settled. We have a comprehensive plan that covers financial, operational, and human factors. I look forward to seeing how these different perspectives align when we reconvene with the data.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Victoria,,I agree. Let us proceed with these selections. I hope the data provides a clear picture of how we can improve our facilities without compromising the stability of our daily academic operations.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Benjamin,,"A most agreeable conclusion. I shall now venture into the archives to see exactly how many ""unforeseen"" rainstorms have historically conspired against our deadlines. I look forward to our next encounter.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
23,1,4,pass,Benjamin,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
24,1,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm ready too! I'll dig into those records and see if the numbers actually add up. Let's find a plan that's honest and realistic for everyone. See you all in the next round!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
25,1,4,talk,Shunichi,,"I'll be waiting. Try not to get too lost in your numbers and diaries; some of us are interested in the reality of the workload, not just the paperwork. See you in the next round.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
