36,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The data is quite revealing. It seems we have a surplus of specialist rooms that sit idle, while general-purpose spaces are in constant demand. Furthermore, projects that benefit the wider campus are rated far higher than isolated improvements.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, that aligns with my findings. Post-occupancy ratings are highest for shared spaces. More concerningly, my data shows that taking rooms out of service requires expensive, off-site hired space, which creates a significant operational and financial burden.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It appears we are all discovering that reality is far less cooperative than the proposals. My findings suggest that any project exposed to the elements is a gamble, with six weeks lost recently to weather alone.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, you're not the only one seeing gaps! I found that mechanical and plant costs have jumped by 20% over the last few cycles. The budgets we're seeing are likely way too low for the current market.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"While you all fret over rain and budgets, I've found something far more tedious. Our bench technicians are wasting hours on manual routines because our equipment is outdated. We're paying people to open windows manually. It's pathetic.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, that sounds incredibly inefficient. If we can solve those manual burdens while creating flexible, general-purpose spaces that serve everyone, we would address both the human cost and the actual demand. We must avoid another isolated project.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, I agree. However, we must consider the transition. If the project requires taking rooms out of service, the cost of off-site hiring and the disruption to the timetable could outweigh the long-term benefits of flexibility.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, your caution is well-placed. Furthermore, my research into delivery schedules suggests that projects driven by ""comfort"" or ""appeal"" are prone to slipping by a year or more. We should prioritize projects with a clear, mandatory rationale.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, I agree on the rationale, but we can't ignore the money! I also found that we have no renewal reserve for old AV kit. If we pick a plan that needs new tech, where is the money coming from?","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, the money is already being wasted on manual labor. We're paying technicians to be window-openers. Investing in equipment that actually works isn't a luxury; it's a way to stop bleeding resources through sheer inefficiency.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, you're right that inefficiency is a cost. However, we must balance that with @Mizuki's point about utility. A project that fixes a technician's routine but serves only one wing may be a poor investment compared to a shared space.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, I agree. We need a solution that maximizes utility for the whole campus while minimizing the need for off-site space. If a project is too localized, the disruption to the timetable is simply not worth it.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, precisely. If we combine your concerns with my findings, the ideal candidate is one that is indoors—to avoid the weather's whims—and driven by a mandatory requirement rather than a mere desire for ""appeal."" Logic dictates we avoid the gamble.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, I'm with you on avoiding gambles! But we have to be careful. If the project involves mechanical plant work, the costs will be 20% higher than the paper says. We can't pick a plan that'll go bankrupt halfway through!","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, your obsession with the budget is almost as tedious as the manual window-opening. If we keep avoiding ""gambles,"" we'll just keep paying for inefficiency. We need a project that actually reduces the operational burden.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, I hear you. We need a project that reduces operational burdens but serves the wider community. Let's look for a candidate that provides general-purpose utility and improves efficiency without risking massive budget overruns or weather delays.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, exactly. We must prioritize a plan that offers broad utility and operational efficiency, provided it doesn't force us into expensive off-site rentals or cause an unsustainable disruption to the academic timetable.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems we have reached a consensus on the criteria. We seek a project that is indoors, mandatory in nature, and broad in utility, all while avoiding the siren song of ""aesthetic appeal"" and its accompanying delays.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, I'm on board with that! Just please, let's make sure we double-check the actual market prices for any equipment or plant work. I don't want us to be surprised by a huge bill later!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, your anxiety is noted. But let's be clear: the most expensive option is the one that keeps our staff trapped in the dark ages of manual labor. I'm ready to see the candidates.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
