61,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Looking at the options, Candidate A aligns perfectly with the demand for general-purpose space and broad utility. It's indoors, avoiding weather risks, and serves the entire campus community rather than a single department.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, Candidate A is appealing, but we must check if the conversion requires taking the hall out of service. If it does, the off-site hiring costs and timetable disruptions could be significant.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, a fair point. However, Candidate C is an absolute non-starter; it is entirely exposed to the elements, and my data suggests that would be a recipe for a scheduling disaster.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, I totally agree about C! But look at D—it's all mechanical and ventilation plant. My data shows those costs are jumping by 20%! Candidate D could easily blow the budget and leave us stranded.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, your fear of a 20% increase is trivial compared to the absurdity of our current situation. Candidate D is the only one that actually addresses the manual labor crisis I uncovered. It's a necessity, not a luxury.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, I understand the urgency, but Candidate D is highly localized. My data shows that projects benefiting only one area are rated lowest by users. Candidate A provides the broad utility the campus actually lacks.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, I agree. Candidate B also offers broad utility, but Candidate A's conversion of an underused hall likely minimizes the need for off-site rentals compared to the extensive work required for D.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, precisely. Candidate B, while indoors, feels like a project of ""appeal"" rather than necessity. My data warns that such projects are the most likely to slip. Candidate A is a safer, more logical bet.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, I agree that A is safer! Candidate B needs AV kit, and I found we have no renewal reserve for that. We'd be starting with a financial hole. A seems the most honest and realistic choice.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, your ""honest"" choice is just the path of least resistance. Candidate A is a fancy lounge. Candidate D stops our technicians from acting like manual laborers. We can't prioritize study pods over basic operational sanity.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, it is not about the path of least resistance, but about the greatest good. Candidate A addresses a systemic shortage of space that affects everyone, whereas D is a localized fix. We must prioritize the community.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, I sympathize with the staff, but we cannot ignore the operational cost of Candidate D. Replacing ventilation throughout shared labs would likely take multiple rooms out of service, forcing expensive off-site rentals and disrupting the entire timetable.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, you've hit the nail on the head. Candidate D is a logistical nightmare waiting to happen. Between the budget volatility and the scheduling risks, it is a gamble I simply cannot support. Candidate A remains the most rational choice.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, exactly! Candidate A is the only one that doesn't feel like a financial trap. No huge plant costs, no missing AV reserves, and no weather risks. It's the most realistic plan we've got!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Kenji, your definition of ""realistic"" is just a fancy word for ""ignoring the problem."" You're all so enamored with your ""broad utility"" that you're happy to let the staff drown in manual labor. I'm voting for D.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Mizuki,,"@Shunichi, I truly care about the staff's burden, but we must be logical. Candidate A solves a campus-wide crisis and carries the lowest risk. For the stability and benefit of all, I vote for Candidate A.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Victoria,,"@Shunichi, I understand your frustration, but the risk of severe timetable disruption and the cost of off-site rentals for Candidate D are too high. For operational stability and broad utility, I vote for Candidate A.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Shunichi, while I admire your passion for the staff, I cannot endorse a project that invites such chaos. Candidate A is indoors, low-risk, and logically sound. To avoid another scheduling tragedy, I vote for Candidate A.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"@Shunichi, I really wish we could help the staff, but we can't pick a plan that's going to crash the budget. Candidate A is the only one that's actually realistic. I vote for Candidate A!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,It's a fascinating display of collective avoidance. You've all agreed to build a lounge while the engine room is falling apart. I'll stand by the people actually doing the work. I vote for Candidate D.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
